!c icesheet thickness change over time based on the power function of temperature, exponent, and ratio
!c  definition of column of ice boundary condition, each boundary type has five parameters, 
!c  the first column is time, followed by 5 parameters for each boundary type
!c  e.g., 
!c  'gradient' ice boundary type
!c        columns: time, thick_grad, thick_slope_grad, rdummy, rdummy, rdummy
!c  'curve-fitting' ice boundary type
!c        columns: time, a, b, c, d, e
!c        where a is sea level [m], b is sea level change per temperature change [m/T], 
!c        c is ice thickness change per sea level change [m/m], d is the threshold of sea level
!c        change to form ice sheet for the specified elevation [m], and e is the threshold of
!c        elevation to form ice sheet!c icesheet thickness change over time based on the power function of temperature, exponent, and ratio
!c  definition of column of ice boundary condition, each boundary type has five parameters, 
!c  the first column is time, followed by 5 parameters for each boundary type
!c  e.g., 
!c  'gradient' ice boundary type
!c        columns: time, thick_grad, thick_slope_grad, rdummy, rdummy, rdummy
!c  'curve-fitting' ice boundary type
!c        columns: time, a, b, c, d, e
!c        where a is sea level [m], b is sea level change per temperature change [m/T], 
!c        c is ice thickness change per sea level change [m/m], d is the threshold of sea level
!c        change to form ice sheet for the specified elevation [m], and e is the threshold of
!c        elevation to form ice sheet. r100 means temperature drop 1C per 100 meter elevation gain [m/T].
!c  'formula': ice thickness = max(min(a-d,0)*c-(z-e)/r100*b*c,0)
!c        
!c  'first' ice boundary type
!c        time, ice thickness, rdummy, rdummy, rdummy, rdummy
!c Sea level and temperature change in the past 120ka, reference Gordan Stuhne and W. R. Peltier, 2016, 
!c Sensitivity Analyses of Surface Boundary Conditions During Long-Term Climate Change, 2016, pp3, figure 1.
!c Year	a	b	c	d	e	a	b	c	d	e
!c the following is for test purpose
